Really, there isn't a magic secret to learning new sounds. It helps  
to practice a lot, especially the kind of practice that makes you  
feel like an idiot where you just say the sounds over and over.  
Learning some of the technical aspects can help you place the sounds  
more accurately. This is the aspect of language learning that is  
really best when you have a native speaker to talk back and forth  
with who can correct you in person.

